    thinking: "**Inspecting Source Files**\n\nI\'m now diving into the source files. I\'m focusing on defining crucial types within `/src/types.ts` to accommodate services, coupons, reviews, troubleshooting trees, SEER calculations, and booking requests. Additionally, I\'m fleshing out `/src/data/hvacData.ts` to include a comprehensive services list, directly correlating to the photo and code, such as AC Installation, Repair, and Maintenance.\n\n\n**Developing Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve expanded the `hvacData.ts` file to include detailed service offerings (Heating Repair, Heat Pump Replacement, etc.) complete with pricing, image URLs, and specifications. I am also working on interactive troubleshooting trees, which will include instant diagnoses, cost estimations, and booking options. I am also building the SEER energy savings calculator to calculate savings based on variables like tonnage, cooling hours, and electricity cost, and comparing old SEER vs new high-efficiency SEER. I\'m also now adding maintenance plan benefits, testimonials, digital coupons, and certifications.\n\n\n**Constructing User Interface**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components. `/src/components/TopBar.tsx` will feature a live dispatch banner and a service area selector. I\'m building `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` for sticky navigation with links to key sections, a phone CTA, and a \"Book Online\" button. Also, I\'m working on the hero section `/src/components/HeroSection.tsx`, which will include an HVAC background image, a high-impact headline, direct CTA buttons, and trust checkpoints with a quick dispatch booking widget.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in UI component construction. I\'ve got the interactive SEER savings calculator with the animated gauge and savings display nearing completion. I\'m also actively building the services grid and carousel with \"Read More\" and instant booking integration. The Maintenance Plan Benefits section, with enrollment CTA, is in progress.\n\n\n"
