  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m deep diving into building the interactive and visual elements. The focus is now on meticulously translating the design into code. I\'m starting by listing the necessary components, with `src/components/TopBar.tsx` up first. This TopBar will be where the \"Live Dispatch\" text will be rendered. I want to make sure this meets the exact aesthetic and functional requirements.\n\n\n**Defining Navbar Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the components for the navbar and am thinking through all the links and content I need. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy, with the brand logo, navigation links, and a clear call-to-action button, aiming for a clean and user-friendly experience. I\'m also ensuring the phone link is easily clickable and that the \"Book Online\" button is functional, to ensure the user can reach the desired action.\n\n\n**Developing Widget Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the InteractiveTroubleshooter and SeerCalculator components. I\'m building out the interactive elements, like radio buttons, symptom selections, and the diagnostic result box. The SeerCalculator is progressing with real-time savings displays and the controls for inputting data. I am creating functional components for HVAC troubleshooting and savings calculations.\n\n\n**Adding Service Sections**\n\nI\'m now adding service sections, specifically a carousel displaying our service cards: AC Installation, Repair, Maintenance, Heating Repair, and Air Quality. Each card will have a \"Read More\" dialog with a full description and an instant quote button. I am also working on the MaintenanceSection, highlighting the benefits of a yearly agreement with a matrix of benefits. I\'m focusing on \"Saves Money\" and \"Helps Maximize Airflow\" in particular.\n\n\n**Incorporating Key Sections**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial sections like Reviews, Coupons, Transparent Pricing, and the Bottom Booking section. The Reviews section features a client quote carousel on the left and a \"Rate Our Tech\" card on the right. Digital coupon vouchers are being implemented with copy functionality. I\'m building out pricing cards for diagnostics and seasonal tune-ups, with clear calls to action. The bottom section will include company information and a detailed service request form.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 240265739
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
