  planner_response {
    response: "**Yes, absolutely!** You have a couple of easy ways to do visual edits:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Tell Me What to Change in Natural Language\nYou can describe any visual change right here in the chat, and I\'ll update the code instantly. For example:\n- *\"Change the primary color from blue to emerald green (or navy/gold).\"*\n- *\"Make the headline text larger/bolder and add a dark background to the hero section.\"*\n- *\"Change the company name to [Your Brand Name] and phone number to [Your Number].\"*\n- *\"Rearrange the sections so the coupons appear right under the hero.\"*\n- *\"Remove the SEER calculator and replace it with a simple 3-step quote form.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Use AI Studio\'s Built-in Element Selection / Focus Mode\n1. In the live preview panel on your screen, click on any element (or use the visual inspector/selector icon).\n2. Type what you want to change for that specific section (e.g. *\"Make this button rounded with a red glow\"* or *\"Change this price to $69\"*).\n3. I will update the code to match your selection.\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Direct Visual Editing in GoHighLevel\nOnce you copy and paste the code into GoHighLevel:\n- If you paste it into a **Custom JS/HTML** element, you can change the text, colors, phone numbers, or coupons directly in the code or use GHL\'s native section styling around it.\n\n---\n\n**What visual elements would you like to tweak or customize right now?** (e.g., colors, layout, fonts, text, images, or specific sections)"
