  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the simple and clear explanation:\n\n### It depends on **where you host and launch your page**:\n\n---\n\n### Scenario A: If you launch your funnel/website inside **GoHighLevel (GHL)**\n* When your visitors visit your live domain/subdomain attached to GHL (e.g. `yourheatingandcooling.com`), **they will see what is hosted on GoHighLevel**.\n* **Important**: To make GHL look **identical** to the preview here:\n  1. Click **\"Get GoHighLevel Code\"** at the top right of this preview.\n  2. Copy the full HTML/CSS block.\n  3. In GHL, paste it into a **Full-Width Section** with padding set to `0px`.\n  4. Click **\"Preview\"** (eye icon in GHL) or view the live URL \342\200\224 it will render full-width and crisp just like here.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario B: If you launch/share the **AI Studio Web App** directly\n* When visitors visit your AI Studio live link (or if you deploy this directly to Cloud Run / custom domain), **they will see the exact live preview you see right here**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n* **GHL Editor Screen vs. Live Preview**: Inside the GHL page builder editor, GHL often shows custom code in a simplified box. But once you hit **\"Preview\" / \"Publish\"** in GHL, visitors will see the full live interactive page with your lead form!"
    modified_response: "Here is the simple and clear explanation:\n\n### It depends on **where you host and launch your page**:\n\n---\n\n### Scenario A: If you launch your funnel/website inside **GoHighLevel (GHL)**\n* When your visitors visit your live domain/subdomain attached to GHL (e.g. `yourheatingandcooling.com`), **they will see what is hosted on GoHighLevel**.\n* **Important**: To make GHL look **identical** to the preview here:\n  1. Click **\"Get GoHighLevel Code\"** at the top right of this preview.\n  2. Copy the full HTML/CSS block.\n  3. In GHL, paste it into a **Full-Width Section** with padding set to `0px`.\n  4. Click **\"Preview\"** (eye icon in GHL) or view the live URL \342\200\224 it will render full-width and crisp just like here.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario B: If you launch/share the **AI Studio Web App** directly\n* When visitors visit your AI Studio live link (or if you deploy this directly to Cloud Run / custom domain), **they will see the exact live preview you see right here**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n* **GHL Editor Screen vs. Live Preview**: Inside the GHL page builder editor, GHL often shows custom code in a simplified box. But once you hit **\"Preview\" / \"Publish\"** in GHL, visitors will see the full live interactive page with your lead form!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
